# Root .dockerignore — the single ignore file for every image build in this
# repo (ai-service, backend, backend test, frontend), all of which now use
# the repository root as their build context.
#
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, Docker root-anchors a bare pattern (no "**/") to
# the build context root — it does NOT match at every depth. Any rule below
# meant to apply inside subdirectories (backend/, frontend/, ai-service/,
# mobile/, ...) must be written with a "**/" prefix.

.git
.github
.venv
**/.venv
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/npm-debug.log

# Dockerfiles are read directly by the build engine, not via COPY/ADD, so
# they never need to be present inside the built image.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
**/Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore

# Not needed inside any image, and can be large/sensitive
db
database
docs

# ai-service/data/ is one-off OSM data-collection tooling (see EXPLAINDATA.md)
# with zero runtime import from chatbot.main:app, and some of those scratch
# scripts have a hardcoded local DB password — keep it out of the image
# entirely rather than baking that into an image layer.
ai-service/data
ai-service/tests

**/uploads
**/*.backup
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.bak

.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

**/*.md
**/.aider*
tempData
